professional charges and other expenses;
(g)
to invest any surplus fund of the Board as may be available from time to time in such manner as may be specified in the
scheme and also to realize such investments;
(h)
to review the performance of any undertakings receiving any assistance or loan from the fund on a periodic basis;
(i)
to enter into memorandum of understanding or performance contract with any undertakings under the purview of this
Act, on behalf of the State Government;
(j)
to enter into contract on behalf of the Board;
(k)
to exercise such of the powers and functions as may be specified in the scheme;
(l)
to exercise such other powers and perform such other functions as may be conferred on or entrusted to it by the State
Government for carrying out the purpose of this Act;
(m)
to do all acts necessary for, and incidental to, carrying out of the functions entrusted or delegated to it.
